  "crossGenreReasoning": [
    "Select only domains relevant to the goal; do not force every pattern into every map.",
    "When domains conflict, prioritize player control, navigation clarity, accessibility and gameplay correctness before spectacle.",
    "A horror map can borrow metroidvania gating, immersive-sim systemic routes, extraction risk gradients or arena combat loops without becoming a copy of any source game.",
    "Large worlds should be decomposed into nested graphs: world -> region -> encounter -> room/space -> interaction.",
    "Generate and judge both macro topology and local geometry."
  ],
